## Libraries and LTO (ImplementationPlan.md M22.a items 1 and 3, M22.c item
## 8; 5.9.3, 5.9.13, 5.9.15):
## - irsymtab has no dllexport bit, so -shared makes every bitcode
##   definition that may be exported (GLOBAL or WEAK, DEFAULT or PROTECTED)
##   visible to regular objects: LTO keeps it, also when nothing calls it,
##   and export selection then reads the LTO objects' flags; a hidden
##   definition is not exported;
## - on windows-msvc-msil only the dllexport definitions are exported when
##   one exists (plain stays in <Module>: its volatile store keeps exp's
##   call to it through LTO, which would otherwise fold the call to its
##   constant result and leave plain to --gc-sections);
## - on windows-msvc-msil without dllexport, the COMDAT copies of the LTO
##   objects are never exported, by automatic export or by
##   --export-all-symbols (section 12 row 'Q22 as implemented' of
##   2026-10-26; M22 review r2 finding 14): a linkonce_odr inline function
##   (inl), a selectany variable (sel) and an MSVC string literal ('??_C@')
##   stay out of the export class and the symbol table, while the plain
##   definition and a weak definition outside a COMDAT group (w) are
##   exported; --lto-O0 keeps all of them, so inl stays in <Module> and sel
##   and the literal in '<msil>Data';
## - --exclude-libs applies to bitcode archive members: with libx.a(xm.bc)
##   and liby.a(ym.bc), --exclude-libs=ALL exports only api, the definition
##   outside the archives, and --exclude-libs=libx.a exports liby.a's y_fn
##   as well (LTO inlines what is not exported into api); in a mixed link,
##   where a CIL object calls them, the excluded members stay in <Module>;
## - a program linked through LTO binds to a library like one made of CIL
##   objects (late binding runs over the LTO objects);
## - --lto-emit-asm cannot write a library ('--lto-emit-asm cannot write a
##   -shared library; link without --lto-emit-asm') nor a program that
##   imports from one ('<file>: --lto-emit-asm cannot import from a .NET
##   library; link without --lto-emit-asm').

# REQUIRES: llvm-cil-dump
# RUN: rm -rf %t && split-file %s %t && cd %t
# RUN: llvm-as lib.ll -o lib.bc
# RUN: llvm-as win.ll -o win.bc
# RUN: llvm-as prog.ll -o prog.bc

